/**
 * @defgroup DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise White noise
 * @ingroup DspCore_Examples_Generators
 * @brief Demonstrate reproducible, stateful noise generation across block boundaries.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise_Goal Goal
 * Use a fixed seed to prove that processing eight samples at once equals
 * processing the same stream as blocks of three and five samples.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise_Run Run
 * @code{.bash}
 * ./build/macos_arm64/bin/Debug/DspCore_Generators_Noise_d
 * @endcode
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise_Output Output
 * @code{.text}
 * One 8-sample block equals split 3+5 blocks: PASS
 * Zero seed rejected without changing output: PASS
 * Continued PRNG state=3306712617
 * Overall: PASS
 * @endcode
 *
 * Block segmentation does not alter the generated stream, a fundamental
 * requirement when a real-time host changes its callback block size.
 *
 * @section DspCore_Example_GeneratorsNoise_Code Implementation
 * \include Generators/Noise/Shared.cpp
 */
